Topi Linkala <nes@iki.fi> wrote:

> A fountain is a mechanism that circulates the same water around for 
> beautiful effect, unless it is used as a synonym for a spring.

What amazing arrogance to relegate thousands of years of ornamental 
fountains to the status of springs! The Romans knew how to transport water 
over long distances then supply it at pressure to spray fountains, but in 
your book they were just springs? And then you have the Moors, renaissance 
Italy, France and probably many other cultures.

Prior to the invention of powered pumps (and Nethack is basically pre-
technological) all fountains needed a continuous supply of water from a 
source at sufficient height to provide the desired pressure. Water 
didn't circulate round the same fountain although it could of course be re-
used in further fountains at lower levels (perhaps pickaxing a nethack 
fountain should reduce the probability of finding fountains on unexplored 
lower levels or make them dry up on explored levels?)


